each over a list the source may omit, into a list the target requires: where
the instance lacks the list, the mapping writes nothing, and _each has no
fallback to say what to write instead.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	l?: [...{t!: string}]
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	l!: [...{u!: string}]
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		l: _each(v0_0.l, {u: _item.t})
	}
}

BackwardLens: {
	v1_0: _
	v0_0: {
		l: _each(v1_0.l, {t: _item.u})
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0343]: l is optional in 0.0 and 1.0 requires l, which _each cannot produce where it is absent
 --> 1.0.thema:8:3
  |
8 |         l: _each(v0_0.l, {u: _item.t})
  |         ^
  |
  = note: an _each over a list the source may omit is written only where the list is present, and _each has no fallback
